# Board selection for 'crowpanel146'.
#
# Everything else board-specific (element order, mirroring, pin map) comes
# from the Kconfig defaults keyed off this symbol, so this file stays a
# one-line board pick and the verified values live in one place.
CONFIG_CAPSTAN_BOARD_CROWPANEL_146=y

# Back transmit off to 11 dBm, as on the MaTouch.
#
# Same signature: beacons intermittently visible, associations accepted,
# then the WPA2 four-way handshake times out (802.11 reason 15). EAPOL
# frames are unicast and must be acknowledged, so they fail before
# beacons do -- which is why the AP can look present and still be
# unusable. An iPhone that provisioned the other two boards without
# trouble could not complete a handshake with this one.
#
# Two of three boards needing this suggests the common factor is the
# USB supply rather than the boards themselves; if a powered hub fixes
# it, this can come back out.
CONFIG_CAPSTAN_WIFI_TX_POWER_QDBM=44
